# Secrets for the local Worker (`./cf npx wrangler dev`).
#
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# .dev.vars is git-ignored. Everything here is a SECRET — non-secret
# configuration belongs in the `vars` block of wrangler.jsonc, which is
# committed. In production these are set with:
#
#   ./cf npx wrangler secret put PAYLOAD_SECRET
#
# so the value reaches Cloudflare without passing through the
# repository or a deploy log.

# Signs sessions. There is deliberately no default: a value that changes
# on restart silently logs everyone out, and a shared value committed
# anywhere would let someone forge a session. Generate your own:
#
#   openssl rand -hex 32
PAYLOAD_SECRET=

# Send-to-Kindle. Optional: with this unset the feature is switched off
# cleanly — the account page says delivery is unavailable rather than
# offering a button that fails.
#
# Workers cannot speak SMTP, so delivery goes over Resend's HTTP API.
# The sending domain must be verified there first, and its DNS records
# added via `email_dns_records` in infra/terraform.tfvars — Amazon drops
# a personal document whose sender fails SPF or DKIM, silently.
RESEND_API_KEY=
